00:10:38,430 --> 00:10:41,058
Mary: And remember, if anybody
bothers you, what do you say?

262
00:10:41,266 --> 00:10:42,893
My dad's a football coach.

263
00:10:43,102 --> 00:10:45,229
- And?
- My brother's a football player.

264
00:10:45,437 --> 00:10:46,437
Good.

265
00:10:46,814 --> 00:10:47,815
Hey, mom, look.

266
00:10:48,023 --> 00:10:49,525
That girl's pregnant.

267
00:10:50,651 --> 00:10:51,693
Congratulations.

268
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,951
Well, that was revolting.

269
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:01,954
All right.
This is your homeroom.

270
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:03,664
Do you want me
to go in with you?

271
00:11:03,872 --> 00:11:06,583
No. Although I could've used you
in the restroom.

272
00:11:07,042 --> 00:11:08,377
Okay, well...

273
00:11:09,294 --> 00:11:10,294
You have a good day.

274
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:11,648
And I'll pick you up
after school,

275
00:11:11,672 --> 00:11:13,298
same door we came in.

276
00:11:13,590 --> 00:11:15,884
Are you crying or having
an allergy attack?

277
00:11:17,219 --> 00:11:18,219
Allergies.

278
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:19,721
It's probably the ammonia.

279
00:11:19,930 --> 00:11:21,640
Probably.

280
00:11:22,391 --> 00:11:24,685
Okay. Let the learning begin.

281
00:11:34,736 --> 00:11:38,240
All right, everybody,
my name is Ms. Macelroy.

282
00:11:38,949 --> 00:11:40,701
In addition to being
your homeroom teacher,

283
00:11:40,909 --> 00:11:43,412
I'll be seeing some of you
in my English class,

284
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,622
and some of you
on the volleyball court.

285
00:11:45,831 --> 00:11:47,151
Just to give you
a little history,

286
00:11:47,499 --> 00:11:49,626
I've been here at medford
for 29 years...

287
00:11:50,752 --> 00:11:52,147
I taught some of your
older brothers and sisters,

288
00:11:52,171 --> 00:11:54,590
and sadly, some of your parents.

289
00:11:56,592 --> 00:11:57,676
Not much I haven't seen.

290
00:11:57,885 --> 00:11:59,219
Until today.

291
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:02,723
I'm sure you're well aware
we have a student with us,

292
00:12:03,015 --> 00:12:04,975
who, despite his young age,

293
00:12:05,267 --> 00:12:07,060
is remarkably gifted.

294
00:12:07,269 --> 00:12:10,522
And I expect y'all
to make him feel welcome.

295
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:12,940
Yes, Sheldon?

296
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:15,360
Per the student dress
and grooming code,

297
00:12:15,903 --> 00:12:17,362
this boy's hair is too long,

298
00:12:17,571 --> 00:12:18,947
this boy is wearing
sports attire

299
00:12:19,156 --> 00:12:21,325
outside of a designated area

300
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:23,535
and this girl's blouse
is diaphanous,

301
00:12:23,744 --> 00:12:25,621
which means
I can see her brassiere.

302
00:12:25,829 --> 00:12:28,207
Thank you.

303
00:12:28,624 --> 00:12:30,042
I will take that into account.

304
00:12:30,792 --> 00:12:31,460
All right.

305
00:12:31,668 --> 00:12:33,670
We have a few minutes
before first period.

306
00:12:33,879 --> 00:12:36,089
I need y'all
to fill out these forms.

307
00:12:36,298 --> 00:12:36,965
What?

308
00:12:37,174 --> 00:12:38,300
Also in violation

309
00:12:38,508 --> 00:12:39,927
of the grooming code on page 48,

310
00:12:40,135 --> 00:12:42,179
article five, subsection b,

311
00:12:42,512 --> 00:12:44,223
you have a bit of a mustache.

312
00:12:46,808 --> 00:12:49,061
This is a stupid idea.
This boy does not

313
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:50,269
belong in our school.

314
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:52,165
Petersen: Come on Vicky,
it's just the first day.

315
00:12:52,189 --> 00:12:53,989
Why don't we all just take
a deep breath here?

316
00:12:54,107 --> 00:12:56,610
The hell with that. Five
minutes into my math class,

317
00:12:56,818 --> 00:12:58,070
he questioned my credentials.

318
00:12:58,278 --> 00:13:00,215
How am I supposed to control a
classroom when a kid accuses me

319
00:13:00,239 --> 00:13:01,759
of being in breach
of the hygiene code?

320
00:13:01,949 --> 00:13:03,593
Well, Hubert, it wouldn't
kill you to shower

321
00:13:03,617 --> 00:13:06,036
a little more often. George,
you want to weigh in here?

322
00:13:06,245 --> 00:13:08,372
- Well...
- Ingram: Oral Roberts university

323
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:09,373
is a wonderful school.

324
00:13:09,581 --> 00:13:11,381
He said I was intimidated
by his intelligence,

325
00:13:11,416 --> 00:13:12,416
and then,

326
00:13:12,751 --> 00:13:14,878
he offered to be my "leader."

327
00:14:00,716 --> 00:14:02,009
Do you know this sonata?

328
00:14:02,259 --> 00:14:03,259
No.

329
00:14:03,719 --> 00:14:05,178
How long have you
played the piano?

330
00:14:06,471 --> 00:14:07,931
I don't play piano.

331
00:14:09,766 --> 00:14:10,392
Petersen: George,

332
00:14:10,684 --> 00:14:11,724
you got any thoughts here?

333
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:13,352
I certainly do.

334
00:14:15,397 --> 00:14:16,397
Mary, tell him.

335
00:14:17,149 --> 00:14:19,192
It's simple.
We don't have a choice.

336
00:14:19,401 --> 00:14:20,944
Well, you gave it a shot.

337
00:14:21,194 --> 00:14:22,834
We wish you luck
with Sheldon elsewhere...

338
00:14:22,863 --> 00:14:24,781
Mary: No, no, no.

339
00:14:24,990 --> 00:14:25,990
We don't have a choice.

340
00:14:26,116 --> 00:14:27,116
He's got to stay here.

341
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:28,243
We can't afford

342
00:14:28,452 --> 00:14:29,077
private school.

343
00:14:29,286 --> 00:14:30,454
I sure can't homeschool him.

344
00:14:30,662 --> 00:14:32,873
He's doing calculus and
euclidean something or other.

345
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:34,291
Euclidean geometry.

346
00:14:34,499 --> 00:14:35,876
Guess where I learned that.

347
00:14:36,084 --> 00:14:37,419
Yeah, yeah, we know.

348
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:40,088
All I care about is that

349
00:14:40,297 --> 00:14:42,924
my son gets the education
he deserves, so you all

350
00:14:43,133 --> 00:14:44,319
are gonna have to
figure this out.

351
00:14:44,343 --> 00:14:46,219
Coach, can you help me out here,
please?

352
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:47,428
'Cause I'm dyin'.

353
00:14:51,350 --> 00:14:52,768
I'd rather not.

354
00:14:57,314 --> 00:14:58,565
G minor.

355
00:15:02,736 --> 00:15:03,736
E flat.

356
00:15:05,864 --> 00:15:06,864
C minor.

357
00:15:09,993 --> 00:15:11,411
You have perfect pitch.

358
00:15:11,787 --> 00:15:12,787
Okay.

359
00:15:13,497 --> 00:15:16,375
Sweetheart, you should
really pursue music.

360
00:15:16,792 --> 00:15:19,169
No, thank you.
Musicians take drugs.

361
00:15:20,462 --> 00:15:22,839
Is there a faculty
restroom I could use?

362
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:28,552
J” ooh... j”

363
00:15:29,930 --> 00:15:31,515
J” ooh... j”

364
00:15:37,687 --> 00:15:38,855
Cooper, Stinson, you're up.

365
00:15:39,314 --> 00:15:42,150
Hey, look,
it's the dumb brother.

366
00:15:44,736 --> 00:15:46,822
Okay.

367
00:15:52,494 --> 00:15:54,079
Bergdoff: That's enough. Hey.

368
00:15:56,456 --> 00:15:57,616
Bergdoff: Hey, that's enough!

369
00:15:57,666 --> 00:15:58,851
- George sr.: Hey, hey!
- That's enough!

370
00:15:58,875 --> 00:15:59,875
Georgie.

371
00:16:00,377 --> 00:16:01,586
Georgie! Georgie!

372
00:16:01,795 --> 00:16:03,255
Stop! Stop!

373
00:16:06,174 --> 00:16:07,454
What the hell is wrong with you?

374
00:16:12,013 --> 00:16:13,013
You okay?

375
00:16:13,181 --> 00:16:15,142
No, I'm not okay.

376
00:16:24,151 --> 00:16:25,360
Where you think you're going?

377
00:16:25,569 --> 00:16:27,362
I quit. I don't want
to play anymore!

378
00:16:27,571 --> 00:16:29,739
- Since when?
- Since right now!

379
00:16:30,907 --> 00:16:32,033
All right, what is going on?

380
00:16:32,242 --> 00:16:34,202
What do you think's going on?!

381
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,580
You mean Sheldon?

382
00:16:39,541 --> 00:16:40,792
You can't let that bother you.

383
00:16:41,001 --> 00:16:42,127
It doesn't bother you?

384
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:43,935
You got called
to the principal's office.

385
00:16:44,546 --> 00:16:46,381
Yeah, that wasn't so great.

386
00:16:46,590 --> 00:16:48,030
I can't be in the same school
as him!

387
00:16:48,175 --> 00:16:49,695
Well, I don't see
what choice you have.

388
00:16:49,801 --> 00:16:53,555
Right. Ever since he could talk,
I quit having any choices.

389
00:17:00,729 --> 00:17:02,314
I know it's hard.

390
00:17:03,648 --> 00:17:06,443
I'm telling you, as your coach,
quit your whining,

391
00:17:06,651 --> 00:17:08,851
get your uniform on and you
get your ass back out there.

392
00:17:10,071 --> 00:17:11,573
But what about as my dad?

393
00:17:12,657 --> 00:17:14,367
Your dad is having a bad day.

394
00:17:14,576 --> 00:17:16,161
Listen to your coach.

395
00:17:22,042 --> 00:17:26,087
Can a clock be powered
by an ordinary potato?

396
00:17:26,630 --> 00:17:28,131
I hope so, boys and girls,

397
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:31,843
or this is going to be
a really boring episode.

398
00:17:32,302 --> 00:17:33,386
The supplies you'll need...

399
00:17:33,595 --> 00:17:35,305
Why can't we watch ducktales?

400
00:17:35,514 --> 00:17:38,558
'Cause we don't learn anything
watching ducktales.

401
00:17:38,934 --> 00:17:41,686
It's TV; We aren't
supposed to learn.

402
00:17:41,895 --> 00:17:44,814
Two alligator grips
and, let's see...

403
00:17:45,273 --> 00:17:47,108
Of course, a clock.

404
00:17:47,317 --> 00:17:49,557
Missy, go somewhere else.
I need to talk to your brother.

405
00:17:49,903 --> 00:17:52,280
Why don't you go somewhere else
and I can watch duck...

406
00:17:52,489 --> 00:17:53,489
Go!

407
00:17:54,199 --> 00:17:55,367
I hate everybody.

408
00:17:55,825 --> 00:17:58,328
It's time for science.

409
00:18:01,331 --> 00:18:04,334
Hey, he was about to power
a clock with a potato.

410
00:18:04,543 --> 00:18:05,293
Not possible.

411
00:18:05,502 --> 00:18:07,379
- Now, listen...
- Am I in trouble?

412
00:18:07,921 --> 00:18:08,921
No.

413
00:18:09,798 --> 00:18:11,258
Maybe. Just listen.

414
00:18:13,635 --> 00:18:15,262
You're not gonna
make it in this school

415
00:18:15,470 --> 00:18:16,972
if you keep ratting people out.

416
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:18,780
But they were breaking
the grooming codes

417
00:18:18,890 --> 00:18:20,100
and the dress codes.

418
00:18:20,308 --> 00:18:23,270
I saw one boy with a t-shirt
that said...

419
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:24,896
"Bite me."

420
00:18:25,105 --> 00:18:27,315
Yeah. That-that's terrible.

421
00:18:28,149 --> 00:18:29,734
Sheldon, let me tell
you a little story.

422
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:32,263
Did you ever wonder why we moved
from galveston to medford?

423
00:18:32,696 --> 00:18:35,782
No. I tend to wonder
about the bigger questions.

424
00:18:35,991 --> 00:18:37,784
Okay, well, here's why.

425
00:18:38,451 --> 00:18:40,870
Your dad had a real good
coaching job

426
00:18:41,371 --> 00:18:43,415
and I saw some grown-ups
breaking rules.

427
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:44,499
What'd they do?

428
00:18:44,708 --> 00:18:46,376
I-It's kind of complicated,
but...

429
00:18:47,252 --> 00:18:49,092
Football coaches aren't allowed
to recruit kids

430
00:18:49,129 --> 00:18:51,214
from other high schools
to play on their teams.

431
00:18:51,423 --> 00:18:52,549
And you told on them?

432
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:54,759
Yeah. You know what happened?

433
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:57,596
Justice descended
upon the rule breakers?

434
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,473
I got fired, Sheldon.

435
00:19:01,266 --> 00:19:02,976
And I got a bad reputation.

436
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:06,813
Oh. That's why you
drink so much beer.

437
00:19:10,191 --> 00:19:11,401
Just do yourself a favor.

438
00:19:11,610 --> 00:19:13,486
Okay? Go to school tomorrow,

439
00:19:13,737 --> 00:19:15,905
and mind your own business.

440
00:19:16,781 --> 00:19:17,781
All right?

441
00:19:19,618 --> 00:19:20,618
Dad.

442
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:24,289
Are you sad that you got fired?

443
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:28,460
Mostly angry.

444
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:31,838
But yeah.

445
00:19:33,757 --> 00:19:35,216
Maybe a little sad.

446
00:19:43,141 --> 00:19:44,684
All right, let's say grace.

447
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:50,732
Thank you, god,

448
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:53,234
for this food we are
about to receive.

449
00:20:02,285 --> 00:20:03,471
Adult Sheldon:
That was the first time

450
00:20:03,495 --> 00:20:05,372
I held my father's hand.

451
00:20:05,789 --> 00:20:08,458
Mary: Our bodies and bless
the hands that prepared it.

452
00:20:09,084 --> 00:20:10,085
Amen.

453
00:20:10,293 --> 00:20:11,461
- Georgie: Amen.
- Amen.

454
00:20:14,255 --> 00:20:17,425
Mary: Hey, George Jr.,
wait your turn.

455
00:20:17,634 --> 00:20:19,487
Adult Sheldon: I wouldn't
touch my brother's hand

456
00:20:19,511 --> 00:20:21,179
until 17 years later,

457
00:20:21,429 --> 00:20:23,807
thanks to the invention
of purell.

458
00:20:38,613 --> 00:20:40,031
You know what I find comforting?

459
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,240
What's that, baby?

460
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:43,451
In a world filled
with uncertainty,

461
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:45,286
this place will be here forever.

462
00:20:47,539 --> 00:20:49,582
Clerk: Hey, Sheldon,
how you doing?

